    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`). There's only one test class in the project, `AcceptanceTest`, and it passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the soft-match \"possible duplicate\" rule for owner creation. When a new owner isn't a hard duplicate but shares an existing owner's `lastName` and `postcode` with a *different* telephone, it's still created and flagged.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added persistent fields `possibleDuplicate` (Boolean) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (Integer) with getters/setters, mapped to columns `possible_duplicate` / `possible_duplicate_of`.\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `possibleDuplicate` (boolean) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (int32) as read-only properties on the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries them and MapStruct maps them automatically.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 added `assignPossibleDuplicate(owner)`, called from `assignDerivedAttributes` (after normalization and the hard identity-key check). It finds the earliest-created existing owner (lowest id, for determinism) sharing the candidate's normalized `lastName` and exact `postcode` but with a different normalized telephone; if found, sets `possibleDuplicate = true` and `possibleDuplicateOf = <matching id>`, otherwise `possibleDuplicate = false` and no match id.\n\n4. **Schema DDL** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added the `possible_duplicate` / `possible_duplicate_of` columns to the `owners` table.\n\nThe soft-match runs only after the existing 409 hard-duplicate check, so hard duplicates are still rejected while true soft matches are created and flagged with the matching owner's id.",
